{
  "repo": "microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat",
  "number": 6031,
  "title": "Convert the toasts to CSS modules",
  "body": "> Continues the CSS Modules migration (#5997, #6024, #6028, #6030) with the toasts.\n\n## Changelog Entry\n\n### Changed\n\n- Converted the toasts to CSS Modules with `webchat__` class names and their style options to custom properties, in PR [#6031](https://github.com/microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat/pull/6031), by [@OEvgeny](https://github.com/OEvgeny)\n\n### Removed\n\n- 💥 Deprecated the `toast` and `toaster` style set entries, which no longer affect rendering, in PR [#6031](https://github.com/microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat/pull/6031), by [@OEvgeny](https://github.com/OEvgeny)\n\n### Fixed\n\n- Fixed the toaster not mirroring in right-to-left languages, in PR [#6031](https://github.com/microsoft/BotFramework-WebChat/pull/6031), by [@OEvgeny](https://github.com/OEvgeny)\n\n## Description\n\nThe toasts move from emotion style sets to CSS Modules without snapshot changes; a second commit makes the toaster follow right-to-left languages.\n\n## Design\n\n- Classes without rules stay plain strings; the toaster's `> ul` rule is dropped, as it never matched.\n- In Fluent, toasts now use the theme's font, like the error box since #6024.\n- The toaster takes its direction from `useDirection()` (the locale or the `dir` prop), like the transcript and send box, instead of from the host page.\n\n## Specific Changes\n\n- `Toast/Toast.module.css`: toaster and toast\n- `CSSCustomPropertiesContainer.tsx`: 15 properties (11 new names)\n- `BasicToast.js`, `BasicToaster.js`: `useStyles()`, toaster `dir`\n- `createStyleSet.ts`, `StyleSet/Toast{,er}.ts`: `@deprecated`\n- `styleOptions/toast.html`: all options (same on `main`)\n- `rtl/toaster.html`: mirrored toaster\n\n<!-- For bugs, add the bug repro as a test. Otherwise, add tests to futureproof your work. -->\n\n- [x] I have added tests and executed them locally\n- [x] I have added `.changelog/<PR#>-<slug>.md`\n- [ ] I have updated documentation\n\n## Review Checklist\n\n> This section is for contributors to review your work.\n\n- [ ] Accessibility reviewed (tab order, content readability, alt text, color contrast)\n- [ ] Browser and platform compatibilities reviewed\n- [ ] CSS styles reviewed (minimal rules, no `z-index`)\n- [ ] Documents reviewed (docs, samples, live demo)\n- [ ] Internationalization reviewed (strings, unit formatting)\n- [ ] `package.json` and `package-lock.json` reviewed\n- [ ] Security reviewed (no data URIs, check for nonce leak)\n- [ ] Tests reviewed (coverage, legitimacy)\n",
